If you're using an LCD screen with a resolution noticeably higher than
100 pixels per inch, you really want a font suitable for that
resolution.  Switching the screen to a lower resolution and letting the
laptop's hardware do the scaling results in a much uglier output than
finding a suitable vector font and scaling it in software.

Or to put it another way: For playing nethack fullscreen, where
fullscreen is 1680x1050, I prefer a font that takes up about 20x40
pixels, regardless of the physical size of the screen.

